# Specialist entities and derived information

Do not give different kinds of evidence the same “healthy” badge. Show each supplied value with its unit, source and time. Entity platforms define what an entity can do, and each integration decides which values it supplies and what they mean. The [interface coverage register](interface-coverage.html) lists all 45 Core entity platforms and 15 further helper and state domains. It does not say that every integration exposes the same fields or a dashboard control.

<h2 id="environment">Plant, environmental and calculated readings</h2>

Plant is a separate Home Assistant integration. It can combine moisture, light, temperature or conductivity readings with limits the household has set. Name the reading that is outside its limit. Do not diagnose a plant from an icon. A missing reading stays missing. A limit the household chose is not expert advice.

Air quality and other sensors can report several quantities in different units. Show the quantity, value, unit, when it was observed and any scale the source defines. Do not apply a generic percentage or say a reading is medically safe. Binary sensor states depend on the device class. Contact open, moisture detected and battery low are different things, so do not treat them as one red and green pair.

Sun data is calculated for the configured location and time. Elevation or the next rising time is a calculation, not a brightness reading. Calendar and weather predictions keep their own source and period. For weather, see [Weather, environmental readings and warnings](weather-and-warnings.html). For time, see [Locale, units and time](locale-units-and-time.html).

