<h2 id="events">Events, locations and image processing</h2>

An event records that something happened. It is not a state that stays true until the next event. Show its type and the time it was recorded, and do not invent how long it lasted. A geolocation entity is a place supplied by an integration. A device tracker or a person has a different identity and different privacy rules. Follow [Maps, zones and location records](maps-and-zones.html) and [Presence, people and shared-screen privacy](presence-and-privacy.html#ha-ctrl-014-states). Do not treat every point as a person who is there now.

An image entity is an image. An image-processing result can describe one image, the time it was scanned and the objects found. Keep these together. An earlier detection does not show the object is still there. Show confidence only when it is supplied and means something for that model. Keep faces, names and other personal details off shared displays unless the real permissions allow them.

