<h2 id="fallback">Unknown domains and future integrations</h2>

When a platform has no dedicated control, use the native default. Show the identity, the correctly formatted state and the available attributes with clear labels, and explain any unresolved state. Do not infer an action from a friendly name, an icon, an integration name or an attribute called “status”. Radio, infrared and remote operations follow [Helpers and scalar input controls](helpers-and-scalar-inputs.html#operations). Notify follows [Notifications, acknowledgement and alerts](notifications-and-delivery.html).

Custom integrations and custom cards need their own review. The official platform list cannot show what they support. Record a reviewed extension separately and do not count it as a built-in component.

<h2 id="acceptance">Acceptance checks</h2>

Test a limit that is breached while a second reading is missing, a retained image result, an event with no end time, calculated sun data and generated text that contradicts device evidence. Check that every time and unit keeps its meaning. Check that viewing a generated suggestion sends no device request, and that private location or image details do not leak through labels or alternative text.

<h2 id="evidence">Where this page stops</h2>

This is a reference specification, not a replacement for native components. The examples use invented records and do not call Home Assistant. Mapping a platform to this page names its design owner. It does not show that every integration, browser or device has been tested. Keep native state formatting, translations, permissions and event handling. Theme tokens change presentation only.

Record real tests with [Native task accessibility and evidence](native-task-accessibility.html). For layout, colour and type, see the [design styles](../styles/index.html). Keep 16px control text, visible labels, keyboard access and readable names at 320px.

Baseline: Home Assistant Core 2026.11.1 and frontend 20261028.5. References, which open outside this site: [Entities and domains](https://www.home-assistant.io/docs/configuration/entities_domains/), [Plant](https://www.home-assistant.io/integrations/plant/), [Air quality](https://www.home-assistant.io/integrations/air_quality/), [Event](https://www.home-assistant.io/integrations/event/), [Sun](https://www.home-assistant.io/integrations/sun/), [AI task](https://www.home-assistant.io/integrations/ai_task/) and the [Core 2026.11.1 platform registry](https://github.com/home-assistant/core/blob/d8a0dc698c8946b44e455d904000db563cfbf1ba/homeassistant/generated/entity_platforms.py).
